# Implementation plan — Spec 1.12.2

## Summary

Add **Send Email** and **Queue** to the WebOnOne **Email** left-nav group (alongside History and Templates) using the existing **iframe embed** channel. Extend `@webonone/platform-nav` Email sentinels; update WebOnOne icons + peer default; extend Identity/Data path→sentinel maps.

See [02-webonone-email-send-queue-nav.md](./02-webonone-email-send-queue-nav.md).

## Branch and prerequisites

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Branch | `spec/1.12.2` |
| Prerequisite | Email History/Templates embed from 1.9.x; SMS nav from 1.12.1 optional |
| Services for manual test | Identity + WebOnOne + Email |
| New env | None (`VITE_EMAIL_ORIGIN` already present) |
| Packages | Rebuild / type-check `@webonone/platform-nav` before consumer type-check if needed |

---

## Phase 1 — platform-nav

**Goal:** Email send + queue sentinels + four-child group.

**Exit criteria:** Member nav has no Email; main/superAdmin resolve four Email hrefs when `externalOrigins.email` set (order: send, queue, history, templates).

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| Sentinels + helpers + nav defs | `packages/platform-nav/src/coreNav.ts` |
| Tests | `packages/platform-nav/src/coreNav.test.ts` |

**Verify:** package tests + type-check for platform-nav.

---

## Phase 2 — WebOnOne + satellites

**Goal:** Icons, default peer path, Identity/Data maps.

**Exit criteria:** Send Email and Queue load correct iframe paths; satellite redirects work.

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| Peer default | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/shell/pages/PlatformPeerFrame.tsx` |
| Nav icons | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/shell/config/navItems.ts` |
| Identity rewrite | `identity/frontend/src/features/shell/config/navItems.ts` |
| Data parse | `data/frontend/src/features/shell/utils/externalNavActions.ts` |
| Email icons (optional) | `email/frontend/src/features/shell/config/coreNavItems.ts` |

**Verify:** `npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root` (+ touched satellites)

---

## Do not

- Add Dashboard / Test / Providers / Settings to core Email group
- Duplicate Send/Queue UI in WebOnOne
- Add per-route `VITE_EMAIL_*_URL` env keys
- Use auth-code redirect for WebOnOne left-nav Email clicks
